comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T21:22:49.577Z","harness:codex","Start evidence 2026-08-10: all-status duplicate search found the canonical assurance family pm-1jzupz and its direct children; this item remains canonical for stored measurement declarations and source evaluation. Active tranche implements SDK-first persistence, derived arithmetic, built-in source adapters, cost receipts, CLI access, docs, and tests."
  "2026-08-10T23:01:02.643Z","harness:codex","Completion evidence 2026-08-11: shipped a persisted SDK-first measurement registry with item, dependency-kind, graph, validate, health, history, links, provider, and derived arithmetic sources; strict declaration validation, cycle/non-numeric/divide-by-zero failures, and per-evaluation cost receipts with caller ceilings. Focused linked tests passed, packed CLI manual acceptance persisted and queried a real measurement in an isolated project, and the repo-wide release pipeline reached exact 100/100/100/100 coverage with 7,201 passing tests."
  "2026-08-10T23:20:18.965Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review finding 2026-08-11: CI CodeFactor parity measured sourceResult at cognitive complexity 25 against the mandatory 16 ceiling after the hosted analysis refreshed. Refactor built-in source evaluation into typed, nontrivial source-specific functions while keeping the shared dispatch and behavior unchanged; rerun exact coverage and static gates before closing again."
  "2026-08-11T00:55:41.750Z","harness:codex","Exact-head completion evidence 2026-08-11: refactored built-in source evaluation below the hosted complexity ceiling; fixed item population denominators; memoized shared measurement references per evaluation; bounded expression/gate concurrency at 4 and item-history reads at 16; added a 5-second Git identity timeout and explicit item-only context flags. The green tracker test-all receipt includes 7,210 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and zero failures."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T23:01:03.175Z","harness:codex","Measurement affordability is part of the data contract: built-in and contributed adapters must return cost with value, while derived measurements aggregate child cost and fail cycles or invalid arithmetic explicitly."
  "2026-08-11T00:55:42.196Z","harness:codex","A reusable measurement graph needs one promise memo per evaluation: this preserves cost accounting, prevents repeated provider/history work, and makes derived/filter/assertion consumers observe the same snapshot."
